---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StatusBoard from '../components/StatusBoard.svelte';
---

<Base
  title="Live status"
  description="Live uptime and response times for the client websites Paul Roy builds and maintains, checked every 5 minutes from Cloudflare's edge."
>
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Live · refreshes every minute</p>
        <h1>Client site status</h1>
      </div>
      <p>
        Every 5 minutes a Cloudflare Worker requests each site I've built, times the response and stores the result in
        a D1 database. This page reads it back through a small JSON API.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-xray="status-board">
      <StatusBoard client:load />
    </div>

    <div class="how">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Cron trigger.</strong> Cloudflare runs the Worker's <code>scheduled()</code> handler every 5 minutes.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Checks.</strong> All sites are requested in parallel with a 10-second timeout. The response time is
          the time to the first response headers, and the body is never downloaded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Storage.</strong> Results go into D1 (Cloudflare's SQLite) in a single batch, and rows older than 30
          days are pruned in the same batch.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>API.</strong> <a href="/api/status"><code>/api/status</code></a> aggregates uptime and medians, and is
          cached at the edge for 60 seconds.
        </li>
        <li><strong>UI.</strong> This board is a Svelte island that polls the API once a minute.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="muted">
        The list of sites comes from the same markdown files that generate the case studies, so adding a project adds
        it to monitoring.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: var(--step-3); margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .how { max-width: 65ch; margin-top: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 3vw, 5rem); }
  .how h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .how ol { display: grid; gap: 0.9rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .how strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .how p { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9em; padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--text); }
</style>
